msgid "AOT-optimized JAR packaging"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus provides a specialized `aot-jar` packaging type designed to work "
"optimally with OpenJDK's AOT features.\n"
"This packaging type:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Structures the application for optimal AOT class loading"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Delegates all class loading to the JDK's class loaders (required for AOT to "
"work effectively as Leyden currently does not support custom class loaders)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Caches frequently-accessed resources (like service loader files) to avoid "
"classpath scanning at runtime"
msgstr ""

msgid "Generating the AOT cache"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable AOT cache generation with:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On JDK 24+, this generates an `app.aot` file in `target/quarkus-app/` for "
"Maven and `build/quarkus-app/` for Gradle."
msgstr ""

msgid "Training with integration tests"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For optimal results, the AOT cache should be \"trained\" by running actual "
"application workloads.\n"
"Quarkus can use your `@QuarkusIntegrationTest` test suite for this training:"
msgstr ""

msgid "With this approach:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus builds the application"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Integration tests (i.e. tests that are annotated with "
"`@QuarkusIntegrationTest`) run against the application with AOT training "
"enabled"
msgstr ""

msgid "The JVM captures profiling data during the test run"
msgstr ""

msgid "An optimized `app.aot` cache is generated"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The more representative your integration tests are of production traffic, "
"the more effective the AOT cache will be."
msgstr ""

msgid "For this approach to work, the integration tests must not be skipped."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With a Maven project generated by our tooling, integration tests are "
"disabled by default and only run for native builds.\n"
"Enable them with `-DskipITs=false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Controlling the training phase"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus.package.jar.aot.phase` configuration controls when training "
"occurs:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`auto` (default): Uses `integration-tests` for Leyden AOT"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`build`: Generates the cache during build (very limited training, faster "
"builds)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`integration-tests`: Generates during integration tests execution (better "
"optimization). For Leyden AOT, this has the same effect as `auto`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Running with AOT cache"
msgstr ""

msgid "Launch your application with the `-XX:AOTCache` JVM flag:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can obtain more information about AOT cache usage with the `-Xlog:aot` "
"option."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can collect even more information in an `aot.log` file with `-Xlog:"
"class+load=info,aot+codecache=debug:file=aot.log:level,tags`."
msgstr ""

