"After driving some load to the application, stop it. Once the process is "
"stopped, you will notice that the `app.aot` has been created in the same "
"directory as `quarkus-run.jar`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Please refer to [JEP 514](https://openjdk.org/jeps/514) for more details."
msgstr ""

msgid "IBM Semeru"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus also supports Semeru's [Class Data Sharing](https://www.ibm.com/docs/"
"en/semeru-runtime-ce-z/21.0.0?topic=sharing-introduction) AOT features."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the JVM building the application and running the tests is IBM Semeru, "
"then Quarkus will generate a shared classes cache instead of a Leyden AOT "
"file."
